  "project_description": "Back to top \n\n Description \n Forms Steps provides an UI to create forms workflows using forms modes. It creates quick and configurable multisteps forms.\n\nYou will be able to add and mix lot of steps using all the entities compatible with drupal 8 form modes.\n\n This project is born in top of a real business case. The core of that module is in use and all new features will be integrated.\n\n Back to top \n\n Roadmap \n \n Sub modules for advanced features like managing config forms and custom forms without entity, or other entities not compatible with the form mode concept. \n Provide better documentation. \n \n Back to top \n\n Drupal Europe Session \n This module was presented at Drupal Europe 2018.\n\n You can find the detail of the session here .\n\nThe session's slides are available here .\n\nThe full conference is available here .\n\n A few links of interest on the multistep topic :\n\n \n Why Multi-Step Lead Forms Get up to 300% More Conversions \n 5 Studies on How Form Length Impacts Conversion Rates \n Should You Use Single-Step or Multi-Step Forms? \n 10 Rules For Efficient Form Design \n Back to top",
